 "lines": {
  "hook": "A snake just bit your hand. Suck it out, or keep still?",
  "b1": "Your fingers start to swell.",
  "b2": "In the movies, someone always sucks the venom out.",
  "b3": "In a lab test, suction got out less than one percent.",
  "b4": "Snakebites kill up to one hundred thirty eight thousand people a year.",
  "b5": "Keep still wins. Moving pushes venom through your lymph.",
  "b6": "One. Take off rings and watches before the swelling traps them.",
  "b7": "Two. Rest the arm in a comfy position and keep it still.",
  "b8": "Three. Let someone drive you to a hospital for antivenom.",
  "end": "Picked suck it out? Replay it and keep still this time."
 },
